1
00:00:06,261 --> 00:00:08,880
She is now suffering from kidney failure.

2
00:00:09,163 --> 00:00:11,400
At this point, all we can do is provide supportive care.

3
00:00:11,920 --> 00:00:13,600
I'm scared I'm gonna lose my grandma.

4
00:00:13,731 --> 00:00:15,800
I'm scared that I will be left alone.

5
00:00:22,659 --> 00:00:25,240
There’s something I want to ask of you.

6
00:00:25,315 --> 00:00:29,840
Please, don’t be too harsh on Vasin or Chat.

7
00:00:35,078 --> 00:00:36,360
What did you do to my mom?

8
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:37,601
You have to choose now.

9
00:00:37,643 --> 00:00:40,160
Are you on my side or his?

10
00:00:40,299 --> 00:00:42,240
There is no way…

11
00:00:42,368 --> 00:00:44,800
Phob and I can live under the same sky.

12
00:02:11,920 --> 00:02:13,921
[Nakhon Ratchasima]

13
00:02:14,822 --> 00:02:16,625
Company, attention!

14
00:02:19,410 --> 00:02:20,994
Stand at ease!

15
00:02:23,754 --> 00:02:25,434
We’ll serve as the main force,

16
00:02:25,882 --> 00:02:28,636
leading three other forces to surround the capital,

17
00:02:28,858 --> 00:02:30,959
to seize the self-serving government

18
00:02:31,338 --> 00:02:33,914
that is directing the economy along communist lines.

19
00:02:34,501 --> 00:02:36,834
Those bastards will have no place left in this country.

20
00:02:40,426 --> 00:02:42,634
We must reclaim our homeland,

21
00:02:42,912 --> 00:02:44,514
no matter how much blood must be spilled.

22
00:02:45,093 --> 00:02:46,474
We must take it back at any cost.

23
00:02:47,010 --> 00:02:48,034
Will you stand and fight?

24
00:02:48,565 --> 00:02:51,600
We will fight! We will fight! We will fight!

25
00:02:51,792 --> 00:02:53,514
We will fight!

26
00:02:54,141 --> 00:02:55,805
We will fight! We will fight! We will fight!

27
00:03:13,274 --> 00:03:15,634
[Free Siam Movement Launched]

28
00:03:15,890 --> 00:03:18,494
[Unveils Its Principles to the Public for the First Time]

29
00:03:19,560 --> 00:03:21,194
They’ll never make it to the capital.

30
00:03:35,406 --> 00:03:37,400
We decisively defeated

31
00:03:37,752 --> 00:03:40,200
the government forces at Pak Chong.

32
00:03:51,895 --> 00:03:53,440
Read it, come on.

33
00:03:53,460 --> 00:03:55,340
FREE SIAM MOVEMENT DEALS GOVERNMENT POLICE

34
00:03:55,461 --> 00:03:59,300
A CRUSHING DEFEAT AT PAK CHONG

35
00:04:05,914 --> 00:04:08,434
[Khao Khu Ba Irrigation Department, Saraburi]

36
00:04:48,114 --> 00:04:51,300
You Khana Ratsadon bastards are finished.

37
00:04:55,394 --> 00:04:57,395
[Lak Si Railway Station]

38
00:05:07,710 --> 00:05:08,844
We’ve secured this position, Your Highness.

39
00:05:09,427 --> 00:05:10,428
Great!

40
00:05:10,952 --> 00:05:12,844
I’ve spoken with the commanders of each army.

41
00:05:13,435 --> 00:05:15,690
We can now make our intentions known to the government.

42
00:05:18,840 --> 00:05:21,280
Attention! Eyes front! Present arms!

43
00:05:25,057 --> 00:05:26,874
The Free Siam Movement has just issued an ultimatum,

44
00:05:27,436 --> 00:05:29,974
demanding that the government resign within the hour.

45
00:05:30,476 --> 00:05:32,677
They will then take temporary control of the country.

46
00:05:33,558 --> 00:05:34,859
What is the government going to do?

47
00:05:34,972 --> 00:05:36,994
They’ve surrounded the capital.

48
00:05:37,068 --> 00:05:39,480
If word gets out, the people will panic.

49
00:05:55,942 --> 00:05:59,760
At this moment, military and civil officials throughout the Kingdom,

50
00:05:59,846 --> 00:06:02,320
having recognized the threat posed to our nation

51
00:06:02,387 --> 00:06:04,320
and the Thai people

52
00:06:04,387 --> 00:06:06,920
by these enemies of the realm,

53
00:06:07,043 --> 00:06:10,160
shall unite to suppress them.

54
00:06:11,880 --> 00:06:13,040
The Free Siam Movement

55
00:06:13,331 --> 00:06:16,160
has mobilized forces from Nakhon Ratchasima,

56
00:06:16,278 --> 00:06:19,440
Ubon Ratchathani, Saraburi, and Ayutthaya,

57
00:06:19,563 --> 00:06:21,240
and advanced upon the outskirts of the capital.

58
00:06:21,398 --> 00:06:24,760
They have established positions at Lak Si and Bang Khen,

59
00:06:25,062 --> 00:06:27,240
and issued an ultimatum demanding

60
00:06:27,440 --> 00:06:28,820
that the government surrender

61
00:06:29,200 --> 00:06:31,201
and restore power to His Majesty the King.

62
00:06:41,345 --> 00:06:43,374
Mr. Tin! Mr. Tin!

63
00:06:43,510 --> 00:06:45,694
Mr. Tin! Mr. Tin! Mr. Tin!

64
00:06:45,782 --> 00:06:48,374
- Mr. Tin!
- What is going on?

65
00:06:50,204 --> 00:06:51,807
Are we really going to war?

66
00:06:53,553 --> 00:06:55,374
If they really make it into the capital,

67
00:06:55,840 --> 00:06:56,841
I won’t let them.

68
00:06:58,321 --> 00:07:00,884
My father said we must stand together to protect the capital.

69
00:07:01,595 --> 00:07:03,520
What are we going to do if war really breaks out?

70
00:07:03,995 --> 00:07:08,024
- What should we do?
- Everyone, calm down.

71
00:07:08,342 --> 00:07:09,343
You need to focus.

72
00:07:09,902 --> 00:07:11,014
You need to calm down, nothing happens.

73
00:07:11,614 --> 00:07:13,574
For now, wait for further news.

74
00:07:14,188 --> 00:07:17,494
Everyone, go home. Take care of yourselves

75
00:07:17,833 --> 00:07:19,614
and your families. Understood?

76
00:07:20,214 --> 00:07:21,934
- Got it, sir.
- Come on, let's go.

77
00:07:23,414 --> 00:07:24,574
Take care, kids.

78
00:07:24,942 --> 00:07:26,294
You too.

79
00:07:27,462 --> 00:07:29,454
I think things are getting out of hand.

80
00:07:30,417 --> 00:07:32,134
The people are split into two factions.

81
00:07:32,716 --> 00:07:34,574
One supports the Free Siam Movement,

82
00:07:34,948 --> 00:07:36,494
saying it will save the country and make things better.

83
00:07:37,070 --> 00:07:39,854
The other disagrees, saying the government has accomplished quite a lot.

84
00:07:41,620 --> 00:07:43,854
I’m sure a major confrontation will break out before long.

85
00:07:46,574 --> 00:07:50,175
I can only hope nothing terrible happens.

86
00:07:51,833 --> 00:07:54,105
I hope everyone makes it home safely

87
00:07:54,404 --> 00:07:55,894
to the people they love.

88
00:08:06,074 --> 00:08:10,444
Grandma, please watch over us all from above and keep everyone safe.

89
00:08:11,434 --> 00:08:13,244
Please don’t let anything happen to anyone.

90
00:08:28,210 --> 00:08:31,354
The government now holds the upper hand.

91
00:08:31,608 --> 00:08:34,874
The provincial troops supporting the Free Siam Movement are faltering.

92
00:08:35,224 --> 00:08:38,008
Should they refuse to surrender,

93
00:08:38,205 --> 00:08:39,514
they will be dealt with severely.

94
00:08:40,648 --> 00:08:41,674
Your Highness,

95
00:08:42,882 --> 00:08:45,014
could the fighting reach our home?

96
00:08:45,483 --> 00:08:47,634
We’re so close to Bang Khen.

97
00:08:53,112 --> 00:08:54,254
We need to run, come on!

98
00:09:24,216 --> 00:09:25,394
Your Highness, watch out!

99
00:09:31,090 --> 00:09:32,091
Your Highness!

100
00:10:00,069 --> 00:10:01,070
Let's go!

101
00:11:07,474 --> 00:11:08,475
Your Highness!

102
00:11:12,094 --> 00:11:13,095
Your Highness!

103
00:11:18,395 --> 00:11:19,396
Your Highness.

104
00:11:19,573 --> 00:11:20,574
Phob?

105
00:11:29,074 --> 00:11:30,075
Let's go.

106
00:11:56,594 --> 00:11:57,595
Please have a seat here.

107
00:12:01,349 --> 00:12:02,350
Easy there.

108
00:12:13,370 --> 00:12:14,594
Stay here tonight, Your Highness.

109
00:12:15,864 --> 00:12:17,648
We’re quite far from the front lines,

110
00:12:18,325 --> 00:12:19,326
so it should be safe.

111
00:12:21,002 --> 00:12:22,914
I'm worried about Aum.

112
00:12:44,108 --> 00:12:45,109
Tomorrow

113
00:12:46,220 --> 00:12:47,670
I will look for her first thing in the morning.

114
00:12:49,094 --> 00:12:50,352
Don't worry, Your Highness.

115
00:12:55,449 --> 00:12:56,450
Thank you.

116
00:13:08,452 --> 00:13:09,453
Ow!

117
00:13:09,710 --> 00:13:10,711
Your Highness!

118
00:13:14,990 --> 00:13:15,991
Please have a seat here.

119
00:13:25,324 --> 00:13:26,325
Did your ankle hurt?

120
00:13:27,260 --> 00:13:28,270
I think so.

121
00:13:32,134 --> 00:13:33,150
Hey, Phob. It's fine.

122
00:13:34,412 --> 00:13:35,413
You don't have to.

123
00:13:35,972 --> 00:13:37,110
Let me look at it.

124
00:14:05,753 --> 00:14:06,754
This might hurt a little.

125
00:14:54,038 --> 00:14:55,150
Thank you.

126
00:15:00,710 --> 00:15:03,590
Thank you for risking your life to save me.

127
00:15:09,686 --> 00:15:11,470
You know I was willing to risk it,

128
00:15:17,454 --> 00:15:18,455
even if it meant that

129
00:15:21,273 --> 00:15:22,274
everything had changed.

130
00:15:27,937 --> 00:15:29,070
Even if both of us

131
00:15:31,766 --> 00:15:33,470
could never be the way we were before,

132
00:15:56,628 --> 00:15:58,430
I would still want to care for you

133
00:16:03,070 --> 00:16:04,590
and protect you,

134
00:16:17,044 --> 00:16:18,310
no matter what role I had in your life.

135
00:16:24,687 --> 00:16:28,510
Whether you forgive me or not,

136
00:16:33,710 --> 00:16:35,470
I will forever

137
00:16:36,702 --> 00:16:39,670
be your Phob.

138
00:17:06,460 --> 00:17:08,630
We’ve secured Bang Khen as our stronghold.

139
00:17:09,550 --> 00:17:11,310
If we can hold this line,

140
00:17:11,601 --> 00:17:13,510
we’ll advance into the capital together

141
00:17:14,609 --> 00:17:16,410
once reinforcements from the provinces arrive.

142
00:17:17,654 --> 00:17:19,430
The news from the capital is not good, Your Highness.

143
00:17:19,708 --> 00:17:21,726
Many people have come out in support of the government.

144
00:17:22,222 --> 00:17:25,830
Our troops are growing weary, and several units have suffered casualties.

145
00:17:26,980 --> 00:17:30,070
Some are beginning to wonder whether we can really win.

146
00:17:33,390 --> 00:17:34,391
Listen carefully.

147
00:17:35,886 --> 00:17:38,270
We’ve come too far to turn back now.

148
00:17:39,750 --> 00:17:41,270
What we have to do now is

149
00:17:41,710 --> 00:17:43,750
we must hold the front line

150
00:17:44,641 --> 00:17:46,841
and wait for reinforcements from the provinces.

151
00:17:47,642 --> 00:17:49,270
Victory must be ours—

152
00:17:49,876 --> 00:17:51,950
not for our own sake,

153
00:17:52,670 --> 00:17:53,790
but for Siam.

154
00:18:20,966 --> 00:18:21,967
Aum!

155
00:18:22,989 --> 00:18:24,790
- Aum!
- Prince Tinnakorn!

156
00:18:30,809 --> 00:18:32,910
- Oh, Your Highness.
- It's okay.

157
00:18:37,004 --> 00:18:38,070
How are you?

158
00:18:38,182 --> 00:18:41,470
I'm okay. How are you? Did you hurt?

159
00:18:42,270 --> 00:18:43,271
I'm fine.

160
00:18:46,025 --> 00:18:47,026
Aum,

161
00:18:48,228 --> 00:18:49,229
I think…

162
00:18:50,174 --> 00:18:52,270
you should freshen up and get some rest.

163
00:18:53,028 --> 00:18:54,029
Yeah, I think I should.

164
00:19:03,913 --> 00:19:04,914
Phob, thank you.

165
00:19:14,129 --> 00:19:15,130
Is everything okay?

166
00:19:18,273 --> 00:19:19,750
I have received orders

167
00:19:22,369 --> 00:19:24,150
to lead the troops to Bang Khen tomorrow.

168
00:19:27,526 --> 00:19:29,950
Prince Vasin and Prince Chatthorn are there.

169
00:19:31,630 --> 00:19:33,110
How is the situation now, Phob?

170
00:19:34,457 --> 00:19:35,830
We still don’t know how this will end,

171
00:19:37,710 --> 00:19:39,150
but I’ve received reports that

172
00:19:40,390 --> 00:19:42,230
the Free Siam side is running into trouble.

173
00:19:44,505 --> 00:19:45,590
Several members of the royal family

174
00:19:46,205 --> 00:19:48,830
have no experience leading troops in the field,

175
00:19:50,137 --> 00:19:51,710
which has led to repeated mistakes.

176
00:19:53,630 --> 00:19:54,810
What about my dad and my brother?

177
00:19:59,726 --> 00:20:00,950
Don't your worry.

178
00:20:01,358 --> 00:20:03,110
I promised your grandma

179
00:20:05,801 --> 00:20:08,070
that I would never hurt Prince Vasin

180
00:20:08,361 --> 00:20:09,362
and Prince Chatthorn.

181
00:20:12,236 --> 00:20:14,550
- Even if it costs me my life--
- Don't say that.

182
00:20:19,430 --> 00:20:20,670
Can you please stop talking about death?

183
00:20:22,129 --> 00:20:23,130
Please?

184
00:20:27,190 --> 00:20:29,191
I’ve already lost my grandma.

185
00:20:32,785 --> 00:20:34,390
I don’t want to lose anyone else.

186
00:21:18,190 --> 00:21:19,191
Phob.

187
00:21:22,430 --> 00:21:24,031
Promise me one thing.

188
00:21:31,342 --> 00:21:33,630
Promise me that you will come back.

189
00:21:47,436 --> 00:21:48,470
I promise.

190
00:21:51,036 --> 00:21:52,137
I promise

191
00:21:53,910 --> 00:21:55,190
that I will come back to you.

192
00:21:57,710 --> 00:21:58,830
Promise me.

193
00:23:43,233 --> 00:23:44,990
Get the villagers out of here! Come on!

194
00:23:58,625 --> 00:24:00,150
Hurry! Let's go.

195
00:24:01,030 --> 00:24:02,430
Hurry! Hurry!

196
00:24:03,646 --> 00:24:04,647
Mom!

197
00:24:07,750 --> 00:24:09,030
Mom! I'm scared!

198
00:24:15,737 --> 00:24:16,738
Let's get out of here.

199
00:24:31,836 --> 00:24:33,691
Drop your pistol!

200
00:24:33,865 --> 00:24:34,866
Come on!

201
00:25:13,001 --> 00:25:14,270
I’ve been waiting for you,

202
00:25:14,890 --> 00:25:16,070
you miserable servant!

203
00:25:42,849 --> 00:25:45,350
You see now?

204
00:25:46,870 --> 00:25:50,371
Someone like you can only ever be a lowly servant.

205
00:25:50,782 --> 00:25:53,350
You’re nothing but dust beneath my feet. That’s all you’ll ever be.

206
00:25:53,654 --> 00:25:54,955
Can you see it now?

207
00:26:01,390 --> 00:26:02,391
That's enough.

208
00:26:04,110 --> 00:26:05,830
Dad, why don’t we just kill him?

209
00:26:06,180 --> 00:26:09,190
A traitor like this deserves to die. Why are we keeping him alive?

210
00:26:10,230 --> 00:26:11,270
He’s still useful.

211
00:26:11,982 --> 00:26:13,566
We can use him as leverage in negotiations with the government.

212
00:26:17,844 --> 00:26:19,030
Do you really think

213
00:26:20,841 --> 00:26:22,610
you’re still in a position to bargain, Your Highness?

214
00:26:25,822 --> 00:26:27,790
I’ve seen your military camp.

215
00:26:30,164 --> 00:26:31,430
It’s overflowing with the wounded,

216
00:26:32,690 --> 00:26:33,910
supplies are running low,

217
00:26:36,130 --> 00:26:37,390
and morale is plummeting.

218
00:26:39,868 --> 00:26:42,510
It won’t be long before your forces are overrun.

219
00:26:43,100 --> 00:26:45,030
Provincial reinforcements are coming.

220
00:26:46,030 --> 00:26:48,431
Once they arrive, victory will be ours.

221
00:26:49,031 --> 00:26:51,950
I won’t let you and your people cause any more trouble in this country.

222
00:26:51,993 --> 00:26:53,710
And who is causing the chaos now?

223
00:26:56,574 --> 00:26:58,410
When we brought change to this country,

224
00:26:59,481 --> 00:27:01,430
not a single drop of blood was shed.

225
00:27:02,900 --> 00:27:04,290
But look at what you’ve done.

226
00:27:05,230 --> 00:27:06,790
How many more people are you going to let die?

227
00:27:06,831 --> 00:27:08,870
Because you used dirty tactics.

228
00:27:09,230 --> 00:27:11,430
You deceived everyone with your schemes,

229
00:27:11,966 --> 00:27:13,550
just like you deceived my son.

230
00:27:14,633 --> 00:27:16,150
I've never lied to him.

231
00:27:17,641 --> 00:27:18,990
I love Prince Tinnakorn.

232
00:27:27,166 --> 00:27:28,167
What did you say?

233
00:27:31,302 --> 00:27:32,303
What are you talking about?

234
00:27:34,822 --> 00:27:37,430
I asked you, what did you just say?

235
00:27:37,823 --> 00:27:38,824
What did you say?

236
00:27:43,350 --> 00:27:44,790
Prince Tinnakorn and I…

237
00:27:46,993 --> 00:27:49,630
- we are--
- It's not true. I don't believe you.

238
00:27:50,742 --> 00:27:51,743
No… no.

239
00:27:52,790 --> 00:27:55,310
No… no, this isn’t real.

240
00:27:56,596 --> 00:27:57,597
It can't be.

241
00:27:57,759 --> 00:27:58,760
I don't believe you.

242
00:27:59,310 --> 00:28:00,870
Dad? It's not true, isn't it?

243
00:28:02,593 --> 00:28:04,110
My brother wouldn't….

244
00:28:04,310 --> 00:28:06,670
No way, he wouldn't do it with a servant like you.

245
00:28:06,737 --> 00:28:09,090
With a servant like you? No way!

246
00:28:09,910 --> 00:28:11,910
Dad! No way!

247
00:28:14,590 --> 00:28:15,591
Ugh!

248
00:28:19,652 --> 00:28:20,653
Chat!

249
00:28:22,886 --> 00:28:23,887
Stop!

250
00:28:28,849 --> 00:28:30,110
We need him alive.

251
00:28:36,569 --> 00:28:38,470
Just wait until we win.

252
00:28:39,950 --> 00:28:41,830
And I will kill him myself.

253
00:29:06,318 --> 00:29:08,510
Your Highness.

254
00:29:10,190 --> 00:29:12,036
I heard that…

255
00:29:12,429 --> 00:29:14,856
There’s heavy gunfire at Bang Khen Market.

256
00:29:15,990 --> 00:29:19,870
Your father’s forces have captured many government soldiers.

257
00:29:20,446 --> 00:29:21,447
Bang Khen Market?

258
00:29:23,204 --> 00:29:24,670
I have received orders

259
00:29:25,390 --> 00:29:27,150
to lead the troops to Bang Khen tomorrow.

260
00:29:28,806 --> 00:29:31,240
Prince Vasin and Prince Chatthorn are there.

261
00:29:32,166 --> 00:29:33,167
Phob.

262
00:29:37,990 --> 00:29:38,991
[Lak Si Railway Station]

263
00:29:39,868 --> 00:29:42,230
We have wounded men! Get beds for the soldiers, quickly!

264
00:29:43,745 --> 00:29:45,070
There are wounded soldiers!

265
00:29:50,038 --> 00:29:52,110
You can’t go in. Please leave this area.

266
00:29:52,977 --> 00:29:54,240
I'm here to see Prince Vasin.

267
00:29:55,910 --> 00:29:57,710
I am Tinnakorn Varakulvatin, I'm his son.

268
00:29:58,390 --> 00:29:59,391
Tin.

269
00:30:00,113 --> 00:30:01,114
Chat?

270
00:30:04,033 --> 00:30:06,034
Did you take Phob into custody?

271
00:30:08,188 --> 00:30:09,189
Phob is here, isn't he?

272
00:30:31,290 --> 00:30:33,150
Did the government refuse to negotiate, Your Highness?

273
00:30:37,890 --> 00:30:39,591
Or have the troops from the east not arrived?

274
00:30:41,625 --> 00:30:43,190
Don’t get smart with me, Phob.

275
00:30:45,465 --> 00:30:46,466
Your Highness,

276
00:30:48,257 --> 00:30:49,350
please order the remaining troops

277
00:30:51,398 --> 00:30:52,640
to withdraw.

278
00:30:56,310 --> 00:30:57,870
Don’t let any more lives be lost.

279
00:31:00,412 --> 00:31:01,413
As someone

280
00:31:03,932 --> 00:31:05,590
who deeply respect you,

281
00:31:07,533 --> 00:31:08,550
Your Highness, please

282
00:31:11,406 --> 00:31:12,510
I’m begging you to retreat.

283
00:31:14,548 --> 00:31:16,710
I don’t want anything to happen to you.

284
00:31:20,174 --> 00:31:21,175
Retreat?

285
00:31:23,209 --> 00:31:26,070
We’ve come too far for that. There’s no turning back.

286
00:31:26,910 --> 00:31:28,550
We must fight to the very end.

287
00:31:35,110 --> 00:31:36,111
Phob?

288
00:31:36,120 --> 00:31:38,230
Tin, how did you get here?

289
00:31:39,596 --> 00:31:40,597
Your Highness.

290
00:31:40,617 --> 00:31:41,618
Why are you looking like this?

291
00:31:45,790 --> 00:31:47,350
Dad, what did you do to him?

292
00:31:50,070 --> 00:31:51,071
Are you okay?

293
00:31:53,006 --> 00:31:54,550
Phob? Chat.

294
00:31:55,252 --> 00:31:57,732
I'm asking you. Please don't hurt him.

295
00:31:58,470 --> 00:32:01,590
I brought you here to watch him die.

296
00:32:01,996 --> 00:32:04,910
You’ll see it with your own eyes, and maybe you’ll stop being so stupid.

297
00:32:05,089 --> 00:32:06,950
Please, Chat. Don’t do anything to Phob.

298
00:32:07,233 --> 00:32:08,234
Please.

299
00:32:10,862 --> 00:32:12,790
- What are you doing? Get up!
- Please don't hurt him.

300
00:32:13,134 --> 00:32:14,935
Tin, get up!

301
00:32:15,070 --> 00:32:16,310
- Chat.
- Get up!

302
00:32:17,671 --> 00:32:19,310
Have you ever thought that

303
00:32:20,372 --> 00:32:23,830
things wouldn’t have turned out this way if he hadn’t come back?

304
00:32:27,550 --> 00:32:29,310
Grandma would still be alive,

305
00:32:29,697 --> 00:32:31,090
our palace would still be ours,

306
00:32:32,690 --> 00:32:34,790
and our family wouldn’t have fallen apart like this.

307
00:32:37,420 --> 00:32:38,710
Stop blaming everyone else.

308
00:32:40,430 --> 00:32:43,270
You’re the one who ruined everything, Prince Chat.

309
00:32:43,710 --> 00:32:46,470
You embezzled public funds, and you were forced to sell our own palace.

310
00:32:46,510 --> 00:32:47,511
Shut up.

311
00:32:47,948 --> 00:32:48,949
You need to shut up!

312
00:32:49,630 --> 00:32:52,310
You’re the one who made everything turn out this way. It’s all because of you!

313
00:32:53,457 --> 00:32:54,458
Chat.

314
00:32:56,844 --> 00:32:59,645
Can you take all your personal anger out on me?

315
00:33:01,140 --> 00:33:02,390
The country’s transformation

316
00:33:03,182 --> 00:33:05,310
would have happened with or without Phob.

317
00:33:07,326 --> 00:33:10,710
But I’m the one who disgraced the Varakulvatin family.

318
00:33:11,777 --> 00:33:12,830
It's me.

319
00:33:13,596 --> 00:33:16,630
If you need someone to hate,

320
00:33:17,558 --> 00:33:18,559
it should be me.

321
00:33:20,044 --> 00:33:21,670
Tin, what are you doing?

322
00:33:22,214 --> 00:33:23,790
I’m the one who started all of this.

323
00:33:24,390 --> 00:33:26,291
If you have to kill someone, kill me.

324
00:33:26,353 --> 00:33:27,430
What are you doing?

325
00:33:27,990 --> 00:33:30,910
What is it? Are you willing to die for him?

326
00:33:32,596 --> 00:33:33,597
If the situation were reversed,

327
00:33:34,633 --> 00:33:38,190
and Phob were about to do this to you and Dad,

328
00:33:39,150 --> 00:33:40,769
I’d do exactly the same.

329
00:33:40,796 --> 00:33:44,030
Everyone here is someone I love.

330
00:33:47,070 --> 00:33:50,190
Please… why can’t we just talk this out, just this once?

331
00:33:50,200 --> 00:33:51,201
Tin.

332
00:33:51,381 --> 00:33:53,780
- Why does it always have to end up like this?
- Tin!

333
00:33:58,366 --> 00:34:00,630
If you need to kill someone, kill me.

334
00:34:06,329 --> 00:34:07,330
Do you know?

335
00:34:12,180 --> 00:34:13,510
All my life,

336
00:34:15,836 --> 00:34:18,870
I’ve tried to catch up with you,

337
00:34:23,433 --> 00:34:26,130
but no matter how hard I tried, I could never keep up.

338
00:34:32,870 --> 00:34:35,390
You were Dad’s pride.

339
00:34:39,556 --> 00:34:42,340
You brought honor to our royal family.

340
00:34:45,838 --> 00:34:47,230
You were everything

341
00:34:48,510 --> 00:34:49,975
I wanted to be.

342
00:34:59,638 --> 00:35:00,639
Chat!

343
00:35:01,484 --> 00:35:02,885
Don't hurt your brother.

344
00:35:04,550 --> 00:35:05,630
He's your brother, don't hurt him.

345
00:35:11,422 --> 00:35:12,710
I was jealous of you.

346
00:35:13,950 --> 00:35:15,630
I’ve always been jealous of you.

347
00:35:17,171 --> 00:35:19,790
Tin, I'm jealous of you.

348
00:35:28,070 --> 00:35:30,190
But you’re my little brother.

349
00:35:35,228 --> 00:35:37,150
I could never hate you,

350
00:35:43,921 --> 00:35:45,690
and I never wanted to hurt you.

351
00:36:16,022 --> 00:36:17,750
The defenses have been breached. Please leave at once, Your Highness.

352
00:36:21,753 --> 00:36:22,754
Dad!

353
00:36:22,905 --> 00:36:24,550
- Tin, let's go!
- Your Highness!

354
00:36:24,990 --> 00:36:25,991
Your Highness!

355
00:36:26,222 --> 00:36:27,790
- You have to run!
- Your Highness!

356
00:36:28,206 --> 00:36:29,207
Your Highness!

357
00:36:30,398 --> 00:36:31,399
Your Highness!

358
00:37:01,457 --> 00:37:02,458
Tin!

359
00:37:03,478 --> 00:37:04,479
- Let's go!
- Tin!

360
00:37:10,890 --> 00:37:11,891
Tin!

361
00:37:18,782 --> 00:37:19,783
Phob!

362
00:37:31,840 --> 00:37:32,841
Tin!

363
00:37:33,033 --> 00:37:34,034
Watch out!

364
00:37:50,593 --> 00:37:51,594
Your Highness!

365
00:38:20,910 --> 00:38:21,911
Phob?

366
00:38:24,193 --> 00:38:25,194
Phob!

367
00:38:31,286 --> 00:38:32,287
Phob?

368
00:38:32,678 --> 00:38:33,679
Phob.

369
00:38:41,286 --> 00:38:42,287
Phob.

370
00:38:47,861 --> 00:38:48,990
- Phob.
- Your Highness.

371
00:38:49,244 --> 00:38:50,245
Phob.

372
00:38:54,134 --> 00:38:55,135
Phob.

373
00:38:55,702 --> 00:38:56,703
Phob.

374
00:38:58,041 --> 00:38:59,190
Phob, are you okay?

375
00:39:02,260 --> 00:39:04,150
Are you alright? Are you hurt?

376
00:39:04,185 --> 00:39:05,186
I'm okay.

377
00:39:05,593 --> 00:39:06,790
Phob, please be okay.

378
00:39:07,394 --> 00:39:08,790
Don't cry, Your Highness.

379
00:39:10,134 --> 00:39:11,790
Your Phob is here with you.

380
00:39:13,662 --> 00:39:15,350
Phob, I’ll get you out of here.

381
00:39:15,726 --> 00:39:17,310
I’ll take you to the hospital.

382
00:39:17,801 --> 00:39:19,150
Phob, let's go.

383
00:39:21,086 --> 00:39:22,087
Is it hurt?

384
00:39:37,185 --> 00:39:38,186
Your Highness.

385
00:39:39,750 --> 00:39:41,550
Can you forgive me?

386
00:39:44,151 --> 00:39:45,670
I told you, I’m not angry.

387
00:39:46,150 --> 00:39:47,790
I understand everything you’ve done.

388
00:39:50,321 --> 00:39:51,440
I didn’t do this

389
00:39:54,716 --> 00:39:56,510
solely for the sake of the country.

390
00:39:58,129 --> 00:39:59,190
Deep down,

391
00:40:01,617 --> 00:40:03,070
I hoped that

392
00:40:05,276 --> 00:40:06,790
if the world changed,

393
00:40:08,524 --> 00:40:10,270
and the class divide

394
00:40:11,174 --> 00:40:12,175
grew narrower,

395
00:40:14,294 --> 00:40:15,550
things between us

396
00:40:17,404 --> 00:40:18,750
might become easier.

397
00:40:21,827 --> 00:40:22,828
We…

398
00:40:24,942 --> 00:40:27,390
we wouldn’t have to hide our love,

399
00:40:30,356 --> 00:40:31,950
and we wouldn’t have to be torn apart.

400
00:40:32,921 --> 00:40:35,854
I know. I understand it all.

401
00:40:36,830 --> 00:40:38,345
And I'm right here with you.

402
00:40:40,654 --> 00:40:42,870
I'm here with you, please don't ever leave me.

403
00:40:45,705 --> 00:40:47,030
I love you, Your Highness.

404
00:40:49,006 --> 00:40:50,007
No matter what

405
00:40:51,630 --> 00:40:54,750
I will be your Phob

406
00:40:55,652 --> 00:40:56,653
forever.

407
00:40:58,340 --> 00:40:59,341
No!

408
00:41:00,110 --> 00:41:01,990
I'm right here, please don't leave me.

409
00:41:02,894 --> 00:41:03,895
Phob.

410
00:41:07,764 --> 00:41:08,765
Tin.

411
00:41:08,942 --> 00:41:09,943
Tin.

412
00:41:11,684 --> 00:41:13,310
We have to go.

413
00:41:13,433 --> 00:41:14,670
Let's go!

414
00:41:14,700 --> 00:41:16,150
- Dad! Help him!
- Your Highness!

415
00:41:16,420 --> 00:41:17,990
- Let's go!
- Your Highness!

416
00:41:18,227 --> 00:41:19,430
- Let's go!
- Your Highness!

417
00:41:21,190 --> 00:41:23,550
- You have to run!
- Your Highness!

418
00:42:05,465 --> 00:42:06,910
- Phob!
- Tin! Let's go!

419
00:42:11,905 --> 00:42:12,906
Phob.

420
00:42:14,049 --> 00:42:15,150
- Phob!
- Come on!

421
00:42:15,230 --> 00:42:16,231
Your Highness!

422
00:42:19,148 --> 00:42:20,190
- Phob!
- Come with me!

423
00:42:21,890 --> 00:42:22,891
Your Highness!

424
00:42:26,590 --> 00:42:27,591
Your Highness!

425
00:43:04,926 --> 00:43:06,510
I’m not dreaming, am I?

426
00:43:08,476 --> 00:43:09,477
You’re dreaming, Phob.

427
00:43:12,590 --> 00:43:13,750
You’ll wake up soon.

428
00:43:19,969 --> 00:43:21,110
If this is a dream,

429
00:43:22,430 --> 00:43:24,270
then let me remain in it forever.

430
00:43:26,950 --> 00:43:28,190
I never wish to wake.

431
00:43:29,350 --> 00:43:31,590
Then I hope you never wake up.

432
00:44:38,051 --> 00:44:41,270
Right now the unrest

433
00:44:41,521 --> 00:44:42,810
has come to an end.

434
00:44:43,388 --> 00:44:46,910
Government forces have regained control of the situation

435
00:44:47,129 --> 00:44:50,090
and restored peace to the nation.

436
00:44:50,990 --> 00:44:53,150
Those involved in the insurrection

437
00:44:53,326 --> 00:44:55,870
will be investigated

438
00:44:55,927 --> 00:45:00,350
and brought before the courts in accordance with the law.

439
00:45:23,210 --> 00:45:24,270
You can’t sleep?

440
00:45:28,390 --> 00:45:29,391
No, I can't.

441
00:45:44,390 --> 00:45:45,391
Chat,

442
00:45:51,740 --> 00:45:52,790
I am sorry.

443
00:46:02,540 --> 00:46:04,090
Why are you apologizing to me?

444
00:46:09,550 --> 00:46:11,190
For bringing you to this point

445
00:46:12,579 --> 00:46:13,990
and making you end up in prison.

446
00:46:16,900 --> 00:46:18,590
I've never blamed you.

447
00:46:20,233 --> 00:46:22,030
Dad, I made my own decision.

448
00:46:23,390 --> 00:46:25,631
I chose this path myself.

449
00:46:29,158 --> 00:46:31,790
I was the one who led you down this path, too.

450
00:46:35,910 --> 00:46:38,398
- I failed as a dad--
- No, you're not.

451
00:46:46,932 --> 00:46:48,090
There’s something else

452
00:46:48,933 --> 00:46:50,990
I’ve wanted to apologize to you for.

453
00:46:59,910 --> 00:47:01,870
I was never fair to you.

454
00:47:05,393 --> 00:47:06,394
Dad?

455
00:47:10,785 --> 00:47:12,990
I kept comparing you to Tinnakorn.

456
00:47:15,244 --> 00:47:17,060
I was always praising Tinnakorn

457
00:47:18,790 --> 00:47:21,150
and expecting you to be like him,

458
00:47:24,910 --> 00:47:27,830
until I forgot that you were your own person.

459
00:47:30,894 --> 00:47:34,110
It was because I was no good.

460
00:47:35,054 --> 00:47:37,655
I was a disappointment. I was the one who embarrassed you.

461
00:47:39,492 --> 00:47:41,593
But I’m the one who made you believe

462
00:47:42,510 --> 00:47:44,090
you were never good enough.

463
00:48:06,019 --> 00:48:07,020
Sometimes,

464
00:48:11,385 --> 00:48:12,470
I just want to hear you say

465
00:48:16,942 --> 00:48:19,761
you’re proud of me.

466
00:48:41,417 --> 00:48:42,670
I'm sorry, son.

467
00:49:11,518 --> 00:49:12,519
Get some sleep.

468
00:49:15,590 --> 00:49:16,591
Come here.

469
00:50:37,982 --> 00:50:39,750
Tin, how are you doing?

470
00:50:41,609 --> 00:50:42,710
I’m doing so much better now.

471
00:50:43,470 --> 00:50:45,471
The doctor should let me go home soon.

472
00:50:48,548 --> 00:50:49,990
You need to get better soon.

473
00:50:51,102 --> 00:50:53,090
Then we can go visit Uncle and Chat.

474
00:50:55,924 --> 00:50:56,925
Siri,

475
00:50:58,177 --> 00:50:59,710
Have you heard any news about Phob?

476
00:51:02,044 --> 00:51:04,830
Janthorn is searching for him.

477
00:51:05,579 --> 00:51:08,412
Maybe he was injured

478
00:51:08,990 --> 00:51:10,910
and taken somewhere else for treatment.

479
00:51:29,217 --> 00:51:30,390
Have you found Phob?

480
00:51:44,961 --> 00:51:46,630
You found Phob, didn’t you, Janthorn?

481
00:51:55,630 --> 00:51:57,231
He's safe, right?

482
00:52:09,777 --> 00:52:11,510
You found him, didn't you?

483
00:53:27,308 --> 00:53:28,309
Nual said

484
00:53:29,494 --> 00:53:30,510
they found the rings

485
00:53:32,364 --> 00:53:34,150
on the ground near Phob’s body.

486
00:53:37,816 --> 00:53:40,478
So she gave them to me.

487
00:53:42,430 --> 00:53:44,630
She thought I might want them.

488
00:53:58,060 --> 00:53:59,061
Do you know

489
00:54:00,510 --> 00:54:02,550
that he promised he would come back?

490
00:54:10,257 --> 00:54:11,990
He has never broken his promises,

491
00:54:13,212 --> 00:54:14,213
not once.

492
00:54:26,054 --> 00:54:27,055
Phob,

493
00:54:29,628 --> 00:54:30,629
where are you?

494
00:54:33,574 --> 00:54:34,990
Come back now.

495
00:54:35,787 --> 00:54:36,788
Tin.

496
00:54:45,508 --> 00:54:47,870
You promised you’d come back to me.

497
00:54:51,201 --> 00:54:52,470
Please come back to me now.

498
00:56:35,497 --> 00:56:36,498
Phob,

499
00:56:39,353 --> 00:56:40,630
I am sorry.

500
00:56:44,330 --> 00:56:47,110
I’m sorry I stood between you and the happiness

501
00:56:47,905 --> 00:56:49,470
you wanted.

502
00:57:25,002 --> 00:57:26,350
Dad? Chat?

503
00:57:31,033 --> 00:57:32,034
Tin.

504
00:57:33,910 --> 00:57:35,190
How are you?

505
00:57:38,283 --> 00:57:39,284
I'm okay, son.

506
00:57:42,400 --> 00:57:43,401
Tin.

507
00:57:44,944 --> 00:57:47,080
Can you help us out of here?

508
00:57:48,480 --> 00:57:49,520
Can you ask Phob to help?

509
00:57:49,862 --> 00:57:50,960
At least, help Dad…

510
00:57:51,120 --> 00:57:53,920
- I don't--
- You don't have to go asking anyone to help.

511
00:57:56,912 --> 00:57:59,000
We did it, and we admit it.

512
00:58:01,464 --> 00:58:03,000
No one can change our minds.

513
00:58:11,288 --> 00:58:12,289
Phob…

514
00:58:15,320 --> 00:58:16,400
he is no longer with us.

515
00:58:29,576 --> 00:58:30,800
He's dead.

516
00:58:48,070 --> 00:58:50,071
[One month later]

517
00:58:54,081 --> 00:58:56,350
I have an interview with them about the restoration of this palace,

518
00:58:56,806 --> 00:58:59,830
so I thought you might like to come along.

519
00:59:06,740 --> 00:59:08,150
It’s heartbreaking.

520
00:59:09,641 --> 00:59:11,289
The Varakulvatin Palace

521
00:59:12,580 --> 00:59:14,090
has now become a hotel.

522
00:59:20,148 --> 00:59:22,430
It’s still a good thing that they at least preserved the building.

523
00:59:24,788 --> 00:59:28,030
Janthorn, thank you so much for inviting me here.

524
01:00:31,918 --> 01:00:33,919
Thank you, Phob.

525
01:00:37,579 --> 01:00:41,200
I hereby appoint you as my knight.

526
01:00:42,537 --> 01:00:43,538
Thank you, Your Highness.

527
01:00:56,822 --> 01:01:00,590
I don’t have a garland, so this cotton rose will have to do for now.

528
01:01:01,990 --> 01:01:03,390
Does that mean

529
01:01:04,593 --> 01:01:07,794
you’ve chosen me, Your Highness?

530
01:01:35,470 --> 01:01:38,030
After all I’ve done, do you still think I despise you?

531
01:02:01,598 --> 01:02:03,790
Whether it takes months, years,

532
01:02:04,190 --> 01:02:05,191
or a lifetime,

533
01:02:06,089 --> 01:02:08,310
I will wait for you and you alone.

534
01:02:10,281 --> 01:02:12,310
I will always be your Phob

535
01:02:13,166 --> 01:02:15,590
no matter what.

536
01:02:33,004 --> 01:02:34,190
Where are you?

537
01:02:35,652 --> 01:02:37,090
Where are you, Your Highness?

538
01:02:37,684 --> 01:02:38,685
Are you here?

539
01:02:39,854 --> 01:02:42,750
Oh my, where are you?

540
01:02:44,240 --> 01:02:45,311
There you are, I found you!

541
01:02:46,876 --> 01:02:49,040
You found me again.

542
01:02:49,953 --> 01:02:53,510
No matter where you are, I will find you.

543
01:03:59,217 --> 01:04:00,270
Phob, is that you?

544
01:04:17,270 --> 01:04:18,630
Am I dreaming?

545
01:04:54,273 --> 01:04:55,274
Phob?

546
01:04:55,478 --> 01:04:57,350
Do you still think you’re dreaming?

547
01:04:58,022 --> 01:04:59,023
Phob.

548
01:05:02,630 --> 01:05:03,631
Phob.

549
01:05:08,070 --> 01:05:09,110
It really is you.

550
01:05:17,294 --> 01:05:19,230
I thought I’d never see you again in this life.

551
01:05:20,862 --> 01:05:22,310
What did I promise you?

552
01:05:23,940 --> 01:05:24,950
That no matter what,

553
01:05:26,478 --> 01:05:27,910
I would always come back to you.

554
01:05:31,638 --> 01:05:33,654
Phob, but your body...

555
01:05:34,726 --> 01:05:36,241
The villagers took me in and helped me.

556
01:05:37,990 --> 01:05:41,316
It took a long time for me to recover,

557
01:05:44,116 --> 01:05:45,364
and I never thought

558
01:05:46,884 --> 01:05:48,230
I would see you again.

559
01:05:49,508 --> 01:05:51,150
- Phob…
- But in the end,

560
01:05:52,030 --> 01:05:53,270
I found my way back to you.

561
01:05:57,369 --> 01:05:59,190
Phob, please don’t ever leave me again.

562
01:06:00,614 --> 01:06:04,001
Do you know how much it hurt to be without you?

563
01:06:05,670 --> 01:06:06,671
No matter what happens,

564
01:06:07,862 --> 01:06:09,350
I will always find my way back to you,

565
01:06:11,518 --> 01:06:13,620
even if I must die a thousand deaths.

566
01:06:14,281 --> 01:06:15,510
Don’t say another word about death.

567
01:06:17,990 --> 01:06:18,991
No more words.

568
01:06:21,537 --> 01:06:22,538
I won’t let you say it.

569
01:06:31,892 --> 01:06:33,540
Your Phob is here.

570
01:06:37,876 --> 01:06:39,030
And I…

571
01:06:40,649 --> 01:06:42,540
will forever be yours,

572
01:06:43,908 --> 01:06:44,909
Your Highness.

573
01:06:46,724 --> 01:06:47,725
Love you.

574
01:06:50,550 --> 01:06:51,790
Love you, too.

575
01:08:39,115 --> 01:08:40,116
Phob?

576
01:08:44,193 --> 01:08:45,194
You're still alive?

577
01:08:49,036 --> 01:08:50,037
Please give us a moment.

578
01:08:59,665 --> 01:09:03,090
It was all a misunderstanding.

579
01:09:04,748 --> 01:09:05,749
The body

580
01:09:06,710 --> 01:09:10,030
was so badly mutilated that it couldn’t be identified,

581
01:09:11,025 --> 01:09:13,270
and Phob’s rings were found at the scene.

582
01:09:14,380 --> 01:09:16,497
That’s why they mistakenly believed it was him.

583
01:09:17,500 --> 01:09:18,886
You’re one tough bastard to kill.

584
01:09:20,193 --> 01:09:21,310
Even Hell wouldn’t take you.

585
01:09:27,294 --> 01:09:28,820
I have news to report.

586
01:09:29,588 --> 01:09:31,561
The government has ordered a reduction in your sentence.

587
01:09:34,001 --> 01:09:35,110
You will not be executed,

588
01:09:36,417 --> 01:09:38,614
but sentenced to life imprisonment instead.

589
01:09:56,558 --> 01:09:57,559
And…

590
01:09:59,172 --> 01:10:01,524
I also wish to beg your forgiveness

591
01:10:24,769 --> 01:10:25,770
for what happened

592
01:10:27,532 --> 01:10:28,910
and for whatever reason

593
01:10:31,078 --> 01:10:32,230
I may have caused

594
01:10:33,198 --> 01:10:35,470
the Varakulvatin Palace to suffer such loss.

595
01:10:38,228 --> 01:10:39,229
You and I

596
01:10:40,420 --> 01:10:42,090
will never see eye to eye.

597
01:10:44,636 --> 01:10:45,670
Even today,

598
01:10:46,406 --> 01:10:48,870
I still don’t believe your ideology,

599
01:10:49,057 --> 01:10:51,564
or what you stand for, is right.

600
01:10:53,297 --> 01:10:55,870
Even if it costs me my life, I will never believe otherwise.

601
01:11:00,420 --> 01:11:02,249
But there’s one thing I believe in—

602
01:11:06,004 --> 01:11:08,470
your feelings for Tin

603
01:11:19,580 --> 01:11:20,590
are genuine.

604
01:11:32,890 --> 01:11:34,150
Listen to me, Phob.

605
01:11:35,782 --> 01:11:38,086
You owe the Varakulvatin family a debt of gratitude.

606
01:11:38,988 --> 01:11:41,766
We raised you and supported you until you came of age.

607
01:11:43,254 --> 01:11:44,255
About that debt,

608
01:11:45,067 --> 01:11:47,073
you'll never repay it in this lifetime.

609
01:11:50,833 --> 01:11:51,990
I am well aware, Your Highness.

610
01:11:54,502 --> 01:11:55,503
Therefore,

611
01:11:58,854 --> 01:12:01,558
you will take good care of my son.

612
01:12:17,260 --> 01:12:20,630
I swear it with my life, Your Highness.

613
01:12:57,796 --> 01:12:58,797
Hey.

614
01:12:59,444 --> 01:13:01,812
Make my brother cry again,

615
01:13:02,729 --> 01:13:03,844
and I’ll break out of prison

616
01:13:04,318 --> 01:13:06,210
just to punch you in the face.

617
01:13:13,438 --> 01:13:15,750
I knew there had to be something going on that night.

618
01:13:36,054 --> 01:13:37,830
Ugh, you two are disgustingly cute.

619
01:13:47,974 --> 01:13:50,316
Your Highness, let's have dinner.

620
01:14:05,294 --> 01:14:06,295
It’s hard to believe, isn’t it?

621
01:14:08,302 --> 01:14:11,198
We’ve been through so much together,

622
01:14:13,652 --> 01:14:15,716
and yet here we are today, still given the chance to be together.

623
01:14:17,193 --> 01:14:18,870
Everything is bound to change.

624
01:14:20,284 --> 01:14:21,285
As the country changes,

625
01:14:22,646 --> 01:14:23,647
so do its people.

626
01:14:25,036 --> 01:14:27,425
The nation must move forward,

627
01:14:29,468 --> 01:14:30,469
and its people

628
01:14:31,153 --> 01:14:34,214
must learn to live together.

629
01:14:36,673 --> 01:14:37,674
You're right.

630
01:14:38,491 --> 01:14:40,710
Nothing ever stays the same.

631
01:14:41,492 --> 01:14:43,950
Someday, the country will change again,

632
01:14:45,265 --> 01:14:47,116
and the world will change with it.

633
01:14:47,990 --> 01:14:51,830
Who knows how far those changes will go?

634
01:14:55,593 --> 01:14:56,862
But there’s one thing

635
01:14:58,225 --> 01:14:59,350
I don’t want to change.

636
01:15:01,745 --> 01:15:02,746
What is it?

637
01:15:04,985 --> 01:15:06,500
You and me.

638
01:15:08,964 --> 01:15:12,790
You once said that if this world had freedom,

639
01:15:14,225 --> 01:15:16,369
our love would be easier.

640
01:15:18,406 --> 01:15:19,790
Do you still believe that?

641
01:15:20,753 --> 01:15:21,754
I do, Your Highness.

642
01:15:22,913 --> 01:15:26,390
Change can never be achieved in a single generation.

643
01:15:29,209 --> 01:15:30,470
What we’ve done

644
01:15:31,220 --> 01:15:33,430
may be only a small step

645
01:15:34,377 --> 01:15:35,478
toward a happier life

646
01:15:36,329 --> 01:15:37,750
for those who come after us.

647
01:15:40,121 --> 01:15:41,230
One day,

648
01:15:42,004 --> 01:15:44,870
love will no longer be hindered by social rank

649
01:15:45,534 --> 01:15:46,630
or differences,

650
01:15:48,985 --> 01:15:50,190
and two people

651
01:15:51,193 --> 01:15:53,571
will be able to love each other without fear.

652
01:15:59,252 --> 01:16:01,759
I don’t know when that day will come,

653
01:16:03,653 --> 01:16:07,070
but we’re fortunate

654
01:16:08,158 --> 01:16:09,470
to have each other today.

655
01:16:12,121 --> 01:16:13,122
Phob,

656
01:16:14,304 --> 01:16:15,404
will you stay with me forever?

657
01:16:18,900 --> 01:16:19,901
Yes, I will.

658
01:16:57,993 --> 01:16:58,994
I’ll put it on you.

659
01:17:13,464 --> 01:17:14,710
I promise you

660
01:17:17,236 --> 01:17:19,750
I will be

661
01:17:20,302 --> 01:17:21,303
your prince

662
01:17:22,910 --> 01:17:23,911
forever.

663
01:17:30,030 --> 01:17:31,031
I love you, Your Highness.

664
01:17:32,425 --> 01:17:33,426
I love you, too.

665
01:18:13,630 --> 01:18:15,631
[The End]

666
01:18:16,857 --> 01:18:18,470
I want Ran Juan soup.

667
01:18:21,175 --> 01:18:22,630
Why don't you try this soup instead?

668
01:18:23,030 --> 01:18:26,630
This mixed veggies soup is delicious. Aum made it.

669
01:18:29,516 --> 01:18:31,030
You two are spoiling him.

670
01:18:32,497 --> 01:18:34,790
You're the best, dear.

671
01:18:34,892 --> 01:18:36,910
May your wish come true, dear.

672
01:18:36,950 --> 01:18:39,470
- I love you the most.
- I love you, too.

673
01:18:39,617 --> 01:18:41,430
Come on, you should put it on. I want to see it.

674
01:18:41,590 --> 01:18:44,230
- Sure.
- This one is quite old. You should stop wearing it already.

675
01:18:44,332 --> 01:18:46,387
I will put it on now.

676
01:18:46,441 --> 01:18:48,350
Here, let me help you with that.

677
01:18:50,724 --> 01:18:52,790
Wow, what a man.

678
01:19:41,796 --> 01:19:42,910
What is this?

679
01:19:43,190 --> 01:19:44,670
What is this?

680
01:19:46,814 --> 01:19:49,290
Thank you!

